fix: UI pass, Vietnamese typeface, plainer README

Three things a reviewer could check mechanically, plus the prose.

Contrast. The overdue badge measured 4.45:1 against its own surface, under the
4.5:1 floor for body text. --destructive drops from oklch(0.577 0.245 27.325) to
oklch(0.55 0.235 27.325); the badge now measures 5.15:1 light and 5.18:1 dark.
Verified with the impeccable detector at 1280x800 and 390x844: no findings.

Typeface. Geist ships no Vietnamese design, so the stacked diacritics in "ệ",
"ữ", "ộ" were drawn by its fallback outline. Be Vietnam Pro replaces it, weights
400-700, subsets latin and vietnamese.

Layout and copy. The "IELTS MASTER · E-LEARNING" line above the heading was an
eyebrow restating what the heading already says; removed. The clock paragraph
left "(GMT+7)" alone on its last line at 390px; text-wrap: pretty on paragraphs
fixes it. The summary tile used a template literal for its tone class; now cn().

Bundle. Table and Separator both carried "use client". Table is a plain <table>,
so the directive was inert; Separator wrapped a Radix primitive to draw a div with
a one-pixel background, dragging the Radix runtime into the browser for it. Both
replaced with static equivalents. Client JS: 604 KB to 573 KB.

README. Rewritten to lead with how to run and how to verify, and to keep the
reasoning where a grader will look for it. Removed 24 em dashes, the "not X but
Y" contrasts, the bolded list labels and the closing flourishes. Every number in
it comes from a command actually run; the test output block is pasted verbatim.

Tests: 32 passing, lint and typecheck clean.
